MID_SE_Max_Dan_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_001: Hope my prey puts up a good fight! Makes it more\nfun to hurt 'em...
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_002: "Fun to hurt 'em"? It's so lukewarm. You should be\nbaring your brutality to the audience.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_003: You got business with me, lady? Better not waste\nmy time—or I'll waste YOU.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_004: Now you're being too cute. It's your derivative\nclaptrap that's wasting time!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_005: And by the way! "Waste me"? A good threat paints a\nmore gruesome picture than that.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_006: Hey, what did I ever do to you? I'm just here\ncleaning my sword.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_007: Well then, use it in the scene! You have a perfectly\ngood prop you're neglecting.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_008: "Got it nice and sharp for ya." Or, ooh, ooh!\n"Got HER nice and sharp for ya." Yes, I like that.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_009: Also, your character—he enjoys killing, yes? So\nexpress your delight! Your twisted jubilance!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_010: "You gonna waste my time, or are we gonna have\nsome fun? My blade's lookin' to play!"
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_011: That's better—but maybe not quite there. But it\ngives it much more oomph.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_012: Look, the impressions are fun, but I still don't know\nwhat you're doin' here.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_013: No, you're right. It's scarier, but...it gestures at "fun"\nwithout capturing the idea.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_014: Perhaps you could compare your opponent's blood\nto paint, and say, "Let's see what picture you make!"
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_015: The visual metaphor, the perverseness of making\n"art" with gore... That has something.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_016: Would you get to the point? I'm kinda busy today.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_017: Oh, my apologies. I should've guessed at your\ndisinterest in dramatics.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_018: What's that supposed to mean?
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_019: Have you not been listening to my exhaustive\ncritiques? Your performance, it's—it's unbearable!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_020: Never called myself an actor. Don't go ragging on me\nwith your theater trash.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_021: You may not be an actor, but you are indisputably a\nperformer, my bepainted friend!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_022: I thought you would appreciate the feedback on this\nboring, thoroughly unscary performance!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_027: 
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_023: Aw, missed. I just wanted an ear.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_024: Not like you need two—since you're not usin' 'em.\nNext time. Heh heh HEH!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_025: Hey, that was pretty good! Was that from something?\nYou certainly sold me on the anger.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_C_026: A white-hot rage that could liquefy metal! You've got\npromise after all!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_001: Heh heh HEH! What's the matter? You better dance,\nor I'll have your guts in the gutter!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_002: No—that's not it.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_003: You don't think it might be a strain, practicing your\ncharacter and your swordplay at the same time?
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_004: Dante? Ragging on me again. I wasn't practicing my\ncharacter. I was...swattin' a bug!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_005: It flew at me, and I thought I'd have a little fun\nbefore I snuffed it.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_006: Oh, interesting! Well, a story sinks or floats on\nthe details. What kind of bug?
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_007: I don't know. It was a bug. What do you want?
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_008: You are performing the role of the clown. You ought\nto engage in wicked antics, play with your toys!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_009: If the bug has wings, scatter them like petals.\nA shell? Crack it like a nut.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_010: Show your delight as you revel in your foes' final\nmoments. That's what will make them despise you.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_011: Heh heh HEH! Fine, then let's start with you. I'll cut\nthat big mouth of yours even wider!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_012: Hm, right. Not bad! I think you've just about got it.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_013: Such a shame, though. I did all this writing—\nunpaid!—and now it's no longer needed.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_014: What are you talking about? Why'd you tear up those\npapers?
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_015: It was a manual I'd written for you on the art of\nperformance. But you have no use for it!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_016: You had a lot to say about my performance before.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_017: I've realized I was trying to direct you offstage, as it\nwere. On stage, in critical moments, you play it well!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_018: When you're at risk of being identified, and when\nyou fight, you make manifest the sadistic joy.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_019: You exhibit the liar's gift. So, no need to refine the\nperformance! Keep up the good work.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_020: The liar's gift... Heh heh heh. HAH HAH!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_021: Yes, it looks like you get it. Well, I'd better go.\nProductive rehearsal!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_022: A lie? Is that all it is? But sometimes it feels like I\nbecome him.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_B_023: Like I am him.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_001: Quite a fine figure you cut! I'm glad I followed the\nmuse here, to your sword practice.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_002: Uh, Dante? We were going to train together.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_003: On the contrary! What I said was I would\naccompany you. I want to research you as Maxim!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_004: Right. What did I expect?
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_005: I will remain a master auteur until I die! But you—\nyou've gone through so much character growth!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_006: In truth, I sometimes yearn for Jester to return.\nIt was a delight to help you workshop the role.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_007: Please don't say that. I didn't like being him—\npretending all the time...
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_008: Apologies—have I hit a nerve?
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_009: Sometimes...I don't know if I was pretending.\nA long time ago, you said I had the "liar's gift."
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_010: But the pleasure I took in what I did—that wasn't\nall a lie. I enjoyed being cruel.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_011: Maybe that performance—the man I became for\nBertrand—was me.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_012: Hmm, you're always so serious now. It's dull.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_013: Wha— I'm telling you how I feel!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_014: Well, allow me to share my perspective. You are an\nhonest, upstanding knight. He is an evil sadist.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_015: You are so desperate to ascertain which one\nyou are, when the answer is simple. It's both!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_016: In the name of justice, you became a twisted clown.\nThen, for the same reason, returned to knighthood.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_017: It's no stranger than a lady wearing an evening gown,\nor a warrior wielding a weapon.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_018: Why feel shame that you enjoyed the role? You did\nwhat you had to do, and that's admirable.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_019: Thank you. I guess—I guess you're right... *sniffle*
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_020: Oh! The knight moved to tears upon acknowledging\nhis long plight alone. This is good material!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_021: No, not alone. You helped me finish my performance.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_022: Why, is that the manual I wrote? You restored it?
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_023: You said I didn't need it, but it's got me through\nsome tough times.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_024: It helped me understand your thinking about me—\nboth of me.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_025: I'd be sad, or he'd get bored, and we'd read it—and it\nmade everything a little easier.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_026: Ohoho! I thank you, Maxim! Seeing the book again,\nI—I feel like a proud parent reunited with her child.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_027: Of course, I never for the slightest moment imagined\nit would help you in that way!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_028: I feel impelled to the writing desk! Shall I write a\nnew primer, perhaps? A play?!
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_029: Dante... You're not saying...
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_030: A new work about the Infernal Clown! Starring...\nthe Infernal Clown! If I can book him, of course.
MID_SE_Max_Dan_A_031: You know, for you? I think he might be available.